  <content>
  <section><title>Activity</title>
<para>For numbers 1 – 3, use the following situation:</para>
<para>Andre’s coin jar contains 85 cents. There are no quarters or pennies in the jar, so the jar has all nickels, all dimes, or some of each.</para>


<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>Write an equation that relates the number of nickels, \( n \), the number of dimes, \( d \), and the amount of money, in cents, in the coin jar.
  </para>
</problem><solution>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    \(5n+10d=85\), where n is the number of nickels and d is the number of dimes.

  </solution></exercise>


<!--START QUESTION 2 -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>Graph your equation on the coordinate plane. Be sure to label the axes. Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course. Graph the equation that represents this scenario using the Desmos tool below. </para> 
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
      <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work. </para>
  </problem><solution>
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <figure><media alt="GRAPH OF A LINE WITH \(y\)-intercepts OF 8.5 AND PASSING THROUGH THE POINTS (1, 8) AND (17, 0)."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/d83b29774019895fb1e20ab3619a1529b88e2e9e"/></media></figure></solution></exercise>  
</example><div class="os-raise-ib-desmos-gc" data-schema-version="1.0"/>






<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE -->
    <para>How many nickels are in the jar if there are no dimes?
  </para>
</problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    17 nickels

  </solution></exercise>



<exercise>
  <problem>
    <!-- INSERT ANY VALID HTML HERE --><para>How many dimes are in the jar if there are no nickels?
  </para>
</problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    It's not possible for the coin jar to have no nickels if the amount of money in it is 85 cents.

  </solution></exercise>

