</example><exercise data-wait-for-event="eventShowMore1">
  <problem>
    <title>Extending Your Thinking</title>
    <para>What are all the different ways the coin jar could have 85 cents if it could also contain quarters?

    </para>
  </problem><solution>
    Enter your answer here:
  
    <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> Listed as nickels, dimes, quarters: (17,0,0), (15,1,0), (13,2,0), (12,0,1), (11,3,0), (10,1,1), (9,4,0), (8,2,1), (7,0,2), (7,5,0), (6,3,1), (5,1,2),(5,6,0), (4,4,1), (3,2,2), (2,0,3), (3,7,0), (2,5,1), (1,3,2), (0,1,3), (1,8,0), (0,6,1)</para>


  </solution></exercise></section>
